# protocol-strings.list — the Italian text that stays in the code in every language (Maat 1.4.0).
# Rule: a protocol prefix is frozen, the human tail after it is translatable. Every Italian literal of a plugin
# script either goes through the message catalog or is covered here, with its reason.
#
# Format: one entry per line, file<TAB>regex<TAB>reason; lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored; LF.
#   file    path relative to the plugin root (scripts/…); fnmatch glob allowed (`*` also crosses `/`)
#   regex   Python regex, searched in each Italian literal of that file (quotes included, as the scanner takes
#           them: quoted strings for bash, string tokens for Python). The matched text is the frozen part;
#           what is left of the literal must hold no Italian, or the line still has to be migrated.
#   reason  why the text is frozen (point of § «Stringhe congelate» of the 1.4.0 plan, then the reader)
# Read by tools/lingua-inventario.py (residual) and, from block A on, by the anti-leak test.
# An entry that covers no line is reported as unused: remove it, or the list stops being honest.

# --- 1. plan-check.sh basis and contract: their whole stdout (basis enters State, contract keys are read by the skills)
scripts/plan-check.sh	nessuna sezione '## Piano di implementazione' \(fuori dai blocchi di codice\)	1: stdout di basis e contract (basis entra in State, cycle-state.sh:235)
scripts/plan-check.sh	basis --write-tests: .*	1: stdout di basis --write-tests (stesso comando di basis, letto da run-phase dopo test-red)
scripts/plan-check.sh	registrata in Approved basis	1: stdout di basis --write-tests
scripts/plan-check.sh	Catena: anello \$k/\$nk di .*|precedente %s \(%s\)|echo (chiuso|aperto)	1+3: riga Catena: di basis (entra in State)
scripts/plan-check.sh	\$\{rec:-assente\}	1: Recorded: assente di basis (entra in State)
scripts/plan-check.sh	Plan status: \(assente\)|Test level: legacy \((assente|duplicata: \$n)\)|Superfici a rischio: |Pavimento: \$s \(riga \$pl\)|Obbligo: \$s — né pavimento né ⚠️|Statica sufficiente: \$s — \$why \(riga \$wn\)|Obbligo: \$s — ⚠️ senza deroga \(riga \$wn\)|Rischio: riga |Piano di test: \$\{r:-assente\}|Tracciabilità requisiti: \$\{r:-assente\}	1: chiavi e valori di contract, lette da implementation-review-cycle/SKILL.md:83-86, prompt-revisore.md:69

